The run this push triggered is `37165185079`, head `45628088`. It finished `success` with
every job green, including the two platform legs. The Windows leg is job `111331251342`:

    $ gh run view --job 111331251342 --log | grep -oE 'test result: [a-zA-Z]+\. [0-9]+ passed; [0-9]+ failed; [0-9]+ ignored'
        suites=33 passed=3485 failed=0 ignored=16

Against the previous run's Windows job (`111285204201`), which is the one that carried the
failure this batch was about, measured the same way:

        suites=33 passed=3482 failed=1 ignored=16

The suite under test moved from `FAILED. 3116 passed; 1 failed; 2 ignored` to
`ok. 3119 passed; 0 failed; 2 ignored`: the red one gone, the two added tests present, the
ignored count unchanged. Section 9 predicted that the ignored count would move by two and
quoted `3116 passed; 0 failed`; both halves of that sentence were wrong in the same way,
because it was written from the `xai-grok-tools` lib suite instead of the job, and because
neither new test is `#[ignore]`d. The job-wide totals above are the numbers to keep.

The three names, from the same log:

    test implementations::grok_build::image_edit::tests::resolve_file_uri_reads_path ... ok
    test implementations::lsp::manager::tests::a_header_decodes_the_uri_instead_of_cutting_the_scheme_off ... ok
    test implementations::lsp::tests::a_file_uri_decodes_back_to_the_path_it_was_made_from ... ok

The second is the test that had been red since the LSP mock-server batch, and it is red or
green on a fact about Windows path and URI syntax that no Linux host can decide. What
section 9 left open stays open: the Windows implementation of a persistent shell, and the
fact that `#[cfg(windows)]`-gated code is still compiled by CI only, so the wine run in
section 6 remains a spot check rather than a substitute for the leg.
